Title: Crystal Palace news: Eagles release new 2025-26 home kit
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [], 'Description': [{'Description': "Amid the news surrounding Crystal Palace's participation in Europe over the weekend, the Eagles released their new home kit for the 2025-26 season.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 105}}, {'Description': 'The launch saw Jean-Philippe Mateta, Marc Guehi, Maxence Lacroix, Eddie Nketiah, Adam Wharton, Justin Devenny and Romain Esse model the new kit, as well as Issy Sibley and Chloe Arthur from Palace Women.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 175}}, {'Description': "New signing Walter Benitez also modelled the club's light green goalkeeper home jersey for the first time.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 91}}, {'Description': 'Palace wore the kit as they kicked off their pre-season fixtures with a 1-0 win against Millwall on Saturday.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 92}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Jean-Philippe Mateta'}]}
